<title>SINGAPORE: Singatronics suffers first half loss.</title>
<headline>Singatronics suffers first half loss.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit/loss	    (2.24)  vs   0.67</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)     (0.92)  vs   0.35</p>
<p>    Turnover		     15.99   vs  55.76</p>
<p>    Interest expenses	   1.73   vs   0.80</p>
<p>    Pretax			 (1.69)  vs   0.13</p>
<p>    Tax			    (0.25)  vs   0.73</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	    (1.11)  vs    nil</p>
<p>Note- Electronics group Singatronics Ltd said its manufacturing operations in Singapore and Batam sustained losses and this is expected to continue into the second half. It does not expect to return to profitability until 1997.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
